# With spaces, project - away is not an operator name (D-026): DS0104 with a fix, and it parses as project-away.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | project - away x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..21
  PIPELINE@0..20
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    PROJECT_AWAY_OP@4..20
      IDENT@4..11 "project"
      WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
      MINUS@12..13 "-"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      IDENT@14..18 "away"
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      COLUMN_PATTERN@19..20
        IDENT@19..20 "x"
  WHITESPACE@20..21 "\n"

error[DS0104]: operator name `project - away` has spaces in it
  --> query:1:5
  |
1 | t | project - away x
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an operator name is one word
  |
  = help: write `project-away`, with no spaces

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | project-away x
which parses without errors
